# Phase 2: GRPO (reward-driven RL, self-distillation retired)

Self-distillation (reverse-KL against a frozen teacher) is retired as of E046.
25+ loss-geometry variants (IS aggregation, SFT anchor, JSD, per-token IS)
all plateaued at 0.69-0.73; the only lever that ever crossed baseline was
context injection (E045, input-signal not loss-geometry). Standing hypothesis
per `STATE.md`: reverse-KL optimizes distribution-matching to the teacher,
not correctness ("sharper but not smarter"). GRPO replaces the objective
entirely: on-policy group-relative policy gradient, reward = the reflector's
existing PASS/FAIL verdict (previously computed every rollout but only
logged, never trained on). No teacher, no distillation, no KL_COEF>0 in v1
(β=0 — biggest compute win, drops the 120b teacher from the critical path).
Implementation: `docs/megatron_trainer/grpo.md` (design spec) +
`plan_grpo.md` (this campaign's plan, repo root) on branch `ra/grpo-live`.
Runs on top of the context-injected dataset (E045's lever) since the context
is baked into the student's own rollout prompt (`prompt` field), not just
the teacher hint — confirmed by diffing the plain vs with-context files
directly.

